  "summary": "The direct matches are the studies applying multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling to predicting customer attrition: [V0211] reports Atlas-ICU accuracy 0.79, [V0210] reports MetroFlow test F1 0.72, [V0209] reports ChurnBench AUROC 0.65, and [V0212] is a deployment comparison on AgriSat-4 reporting MAE=0.86. These datasets and metrics are not strictly comparable, and MAE is an error measure rather than a higher-is-better score. Because exactly five IDs are required, [V0235] is appended only as a same-method control; it concerns predicting road traffic flow, not customer churn, so it is not direct evidence for the research question.",
